NOTE ON INTENDED USE

The MIT terms above are the legal license. What follows is not an additional
legal restriction — it is the authors' statement of what this project is for,
and what it asks of the people who use it.

Voice Designer exists to help people CREATE voices: to sculpt an original
synthetic voice, to shape one toward a character or a feeling, and to give
people who need a synthetic voice a way to make one that feels like their own.

It is NOT intended for impersonating real people.

Concretely, please do not use this project to:

  - Reproduce the voice of a real person without their clear, informed consent.
  - Make synthetic speech that could be mistaken for a real person's recorded
    words — especially public figures, or anyone whose voice is their livelihood
    (narrators, voice actors, broadcasters, performers).
  - Defeat voice-based authentication, or produce material intended to deceive
    a listener about who is speaking.
  - Generate audio that harasses, defames, or sexualizes any real person.

If you are matching against a reference recording, the reasonable standard is
simple: it should be your own voice, a voice you have explicit permission to
use, or a synthetic or public-domain source. "I found it online" is not
permission.

Voice is personal, and for many people it is also their profession. Cloning
someone's voice without consent takes something from them that they cannot get
back. Please build things you would be comfortable having done to your own
voice.
